---
/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   /brief — the free AI Opportunity Brief offer.

   NOT /exposure, and not /report. "Exposure" read as fear-mongering, and the
   URL is the first words a visitor sees. "Report" was accurate and dull, and it
   promised research when the thing being given away is advice. A brief is what
   you hand someone before a conversation, which is exactly what this is.

   TOP OF THE LADDER, and a different promise from the Reality Check. This one
   is free and automated: we read your public surface, find what comparable
   companies have actually done, and write you an analysis. The Reality Check is
   the hour that follows.

   THE COPY SELLS THE ANALYSIS, NOT THE CITATIONS. The first version of this
   report led with sourced facts and a reader's verdict was "a dump of press
   release headlines — ChatGPT could have spit this out". They were right, and
   the fix was upstream. So this page promises what the report now answers:
   where you stand, where you're strong, where you're exposed, what companies
   like you did and whether it worked, and what to weigh. Sourcing is the proof,
   not the pitch.

   The call is framed as course-correcting the report rather than as a sales
   call, because that is what it honestly is: the document is built entirely
   from outside, the boundary section lists what we could not see, and the
   fastest way to fix that is an hour with the people who know.

   Positioning: written to the recommended position in docs/01 — design-led AI
   product studio with a care-operations wedge — and deliberately naming no
   vertical, so landing Decision #1 does not invalidate the page.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------- */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ExposureRequest from '../components/ExposureRequest.astro';

const title = 'Your free AI Opportunity Brief — SeeSaw Labs';
const description =
  'A free, sourced analysis of where your company stands on AI: what comparable companies have actually done, and what it puts in front of you. Every number carries a source, or is left blank for you to fill in.';
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <!-- ------------------------------ hero ------------------------------ -->
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap hero__in">
      <p class="eyebrow">Free · No catch · Yours to keep</p>
      <h1 class="hero__h">
        Most AI advice could be about anyone.<br />
        <span class="hero__em">This one's about you.</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="lede hero__lede">
        We read your website, dig up what companies like yours have actually
        done with AI, and send you three ideas we&rsquo;d build if it were our
        business. Plus the questions we&rsquo;d want to ask you. Every number
        links to where we got it, or we leave it blank rather than guess.
      </p>
      <div class="hero__cta">
        <a href="#request" class="btn">Get my brief</a>
        <a href="#inside" class="btn btn--ghost">What's in it</a>
      </div>
      <p class="hero__fine">
        No charge and no follow-up sequence. One email, one private link.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ---------------------------- the problem ------------------------- -->
  <section class="section section--sunk">
    <div class="wrap-narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">Why this exists</p>
      <h2 class="h2">
        Plenty of people will tell you AI matters. Far fewer will tell you what
        to do about it in <em>your</em> business.
      </h2>
      <p class="body">
        You&rsquo;ve read the generic version already. The useful version takes
        actual work: finding what your competitors have announced and when,
        reading your own site the way a customer reads it, then saying what
        we&rsquo;d do about the gap.
      </p>
      <p class="body">
        We built the research into a repeatable pipeline, so we can give the
        report away. It&rsquo;s the cheapest way for us to show you how we
        think, and the cheapest way for you to find out if we&rsquo;re any good.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- --------------------------- what's inside ------------------------ -->
  <section class="section" id="inside">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="head">
        <p class="eyebrow">What's in it</p>
        <h2 class="h2">What you actually get</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          Our read on your situation, with all the evidence attached at the
          bottom so you can check any line of it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <ol class="cards">
        <li class="card">
          <h3 class="card__h">What we think is going on</h3>
          <p class="card__b">
            A short read on your situation, based on what your own site says
            about how the work gets done.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li class="card">
          <h3 class="card__h">Three ideas we&rsquo;d build</h3>
          <p class="card__b">
            Specific enough to argue with, in the order we&rsquo;d do them. Not
            &ldquo;add AI to your operation&rdquo;.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li class="card">
          <h3 class="card__h">A rough size on each one</h3>
          <p class="card__b">
            Where we can, some arithmetic on what an idea might be worth. Our
            guesses are labelled as guesses so you can correct them.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li class="card">
          <h3 class="card__h">The questions we&rsquo;d ask you</h3>
          <p class="card__b">
            The handful of things we can&rsquo;t find out from outside, and
            that would change what we&rsquo;d advise.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li class="card">
          <h3 class="card__h">What your competitors did</h3>
          <p class="card__b">
            Every AI move we can tie to a dated article, and whether it seems
            to have worked. If nobody in your field has moved yet, we say that.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li class="card">
          <h3 class="card__h">Where we&rsquo;re probably wrong</h3>
          <p class="card__b">
            The parts we&rsquo;d bet we got wrong, since we only had your
            website to go on.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ------------------------ the honesty promise --------------------- -->
  <section class="section section--sunk">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="head">
        <p class="eyebrow">The rule we hold ourselves to</p>
        <h2 class="h2">Every number links to where we got it</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="two">
        <div>
          <p class="body">
            Anyone can write a report full of made-up percentages. So every
            figure in yours either links to its source, or shows up as
            a <span class="blankdemo">blank</span> with a note on what
            we&rsquo;d need from you to fill it in.
          </p>
          <p class="body">
            That rule lives in our code, not in a style guide. If we can&rsquo;t
            trace a number, the sentence containing it gets dropped before you
            see it. The check runs over our analysis too, not just the evidence.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="body">
            There&rsquo;s a whole section on <strong>what we couldn&rsquo;t
            work out</strong>. Your volumes, your cycle times, which manual step
            actually costs you money. None of that is public and we won&rsquo;t
            pretend otherwise.
          </p>
          <p class="body">
            Those gaps are the main reason to get on a call with us. They&rsquo;re
            also how you can tell someone actually looked at your business.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="samplelink">
        <a href="/sample">See a real one &rarr;</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ------------------------------ request ---------------------------- -->
  <section class="section" id="request">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="head">
        <p class="eyebrow">A few things we can&rsquo;t look up</p>
        <h2 class="h2">Tell us where to look</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          We can read your website. What we can&rsquo;t work out is how
          you&rsquo;d describe the business in one line, or who you actually
          think of as a competitor. Those two answers are the difference
          between a sharp report and a generic one.
        </p>
      </div>
      <ExposureRequest />
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ------------------------------- close ---------------------------- -->
  <section class="section section--deep">
    <div class="wrap-narrow close">
      <p class="eyebrow">And then</p>
      <h2 class="close__h">Tell us where we got it wrong.</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        We wrote it from the outside, so some of it will be wrong or out of
        date. An hour on a call is where you put us straight and fill in the
        blanks with numbers only you have. That hour is the AI Reality Check.
        It&rsquo;s free too, and you keep the written assessment either way.
      </p>
      <a href="/book" class="btn btn--on-deep">Book the hour</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <style>
    /* Local to this page. Shared primitives live in styles/tokens.css. */
    .hero { padding-block: clamp(var(--sp-16), 10vw, var(--sp-24)) var(--sp-16); }
    .hero__in { display: grid; gap: var(--sp-5); }
    .hero__h {
      font-size: clamp(var(--text-4xl), 6.5vw, var(--text-6xl));
      font-weight: 600;
      line-height: var(--lh-tight);
      letter-spacing: var(--ls-tight);
      margin: 0;
      text-wrap: balance;
    }
    .hero__em { color: var(--accent); }
    .hero__lede { max-width: 56ch; margin: 0; }
    .hero__cta { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--sp-3); margin-top: var(--sp-2); }
    .hero__fine { font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--muted); margin: 0; }

    .h2 {
      font-size: clamp(var(--text-2xl), 3.6vw, var(--text-4xl));
      font-weight: 600;
      line-height: var(--lh-tight);
      letter-spacing: var(--ls-tight);
      margin: var(--sp-3) 0 var(--sp-5);
      text-wrap: balance;
    }
    .h2 em { font-style: italic; color: var(--accent); }
    .section--deep .h2 { color: #fff; }

    .head { max-width: 60ch; margin-bottom: var(--sp-10); }
    .head .lede { margin: 0; }

    .body {
      font-size: var(--text-lg);
      line-height: var(--lh-relaxed);
      color: var(--ink-2);
      max-width: 60ch;
      margin: 0 0 var(--sp-5);
    }
    .body:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

    .cards {
      list-style: none;
      counter-reset: card;
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
      display: grid;
      gap: var(--sp-5);
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(17rem, 1fr));
    }
    .card {
      counter-increment: card;
      position: relative;
      background: var(--surface);
      border: 1px solid var(--rule);
      border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
      padding: var(--sp-6);
    }
    .card::before {
      content: counter(card, decimal-leading-zero);
      font-family: var(--font-accent);
      font-size: var(--text-sm);
      color: var(--accent);
      letter-spacing: var(--ls-wide);
    }
    .card__h {
      font-size: var(--text-xl);
      font-weight: 600;
      letter-spacing: var(--ls-tight);
      line-height: var(--lh-snug);
      margin: var(--sp-2) 0 var(--sp-3);
    }
    .card__b { font-size: var(--text-md); line-height: var(--lh-relaxed); color: var(--ink-2); margin: 0; }

    .two { display: grid; gap: var(--sp-8); }
    @media (min-width: 48rem) {
      .two { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: var(--sp-10); }
    }

    /* Mirrors how a declared blank renders inside the report itself. */
    .blankdemo {
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 0.9em;
      color: var(--accent-deep);
      background: var(--accent-soft);
      border-bottom: 2px solid var(--accent);
      padding: 0.05rem 0.3rem;
      border-radius: var(--radius-sm) var(--radius-sm) 0 0;
      white-space: nowrap;
    }

    .samplelink { margin: var(--sp-10) 0 0; font-size: var(--text-lg); }
    .samplelink a { color: var(--accent-deep); font-weight: 500; }

    .close { display: grid; gap: var(--sp-5); justify-items: start; }
    .close__h {
      font-size: clamp(var(--text-3xl), 5vw, var(--text-5xl));
      font-weight: 600;
      line-height: var(--lh-tight);
      letter-spacing: var(--ls-tight);
      margin: 0;
      color: #fff;
      text-wrap: balance;
    }
  </style>
</Base>
